SIGNAL = r"""{\sffamily\bfseries\small\color{Deep}A metrology-chain network calibration worked for temperature, humidity and pressure in Helsinki and Antwerp and failed first on PM: feasible only on restricted sensor subsets, because PM signals are localized and weakly correlated.}\\[1.4mm]
\footnotesize
VTT-led; Laplace-domain pairwise transfer functions, a separated spatial term and an overdetermined solve against one reference, with Monte Carlo uncertainty. Helsinki linked to SMEAR III; Antwerp from SensEURCity.
\textbf{Where it is weak:} the abstract gives no PM R$^2$, RMSE or uncertainty, so the size of the failure cannot be graded, and two cities do not bound the geometries where it holds.
\textbf{Why it matters here:} node-to-node calibration transfer assumes neighbouring sensors see related signals. The more local the source field, the more value a dense network has and the less that assumption holds; the property that justifies deployment is the one that defeats reference-free transfer. Co-location does not go away."""

